 "frozen_rule": "Frozen before replay (2026-10-26T02:07Z). No new code, no thresholds: existing opt-in flags only.\nBinary: develop 2e224ea (bin/gnss-solve-dev2e224ea, sha256 c3d42336...5c85).\nProfile P = repository PPC RTK profile, argv exactly as apps/commands/benchmarks/gnss_ppc_native_replay.py:\n  gnss_solve --rover rover.obs --base base.obs --nav base.nav --mode kinematic --no-kml\n             --preset low-cost --ratio 2.4 --max-subset-ar-drop-steps 18 --rtk-snr-weighting --no-arfilter --out <pos>\n  (no --base-ecef: header APPROX POSITION, as in the replay tool; no --glonass-ar).\nRecipes: P; P+M (--max-position-jump-motion-compensation); P+CDM (CD + M); P+CDMH (CDM + --hold-kalman-update).\nCD = --max-fixed-anchor-age 5 --max-fixed-doppler-consensus 3 --low-ratio-guard-threshold 1e9\n     --low-ratio-min-fixed-ambiguities 10 --fix-history-motion-compensation\nRuns: PPC tokyo/nagoya run1-3 (development data). Reference only for scoring (exact 1 ms, eval_ppc scoring).\nSanity (not a gate): P fixed epochs within 5% of docs/ppc_fix_recovery_evaluation.json (8235764f) per run.\nPredictions (mechanism):\n  1. P+M: P already uses a 30 m/s motion-aware jump limit, so M is nearly inert:\n     FIX count within 1% of P on every run.\n  2. P+CDM: the 10-ambiguity floor and Doppler consensus reject weak subset fixes:\n     wrong FIX >0.5 m and >2 m each decrease on at least 5 of 6 runs;\n     P-correct loss exceeds 1% on at least one run (so the gate fails).\n  3. P+CDMH: summed wrong FIX >0.5 m over 6 runs <= P+CDM.\nGate for each recipe vs P (docs/fix_recovery_guard.md, every run): wrong FIX >0.5/2/3 m not increased;\nP-correct loss <= 1% (0.5 m); missing and horizontal P95 not increased; recovery P95 and right-censoring\nnot increased; at least one wrong-FIX population decreases.\nIf a recipe passes every run: report as a GO candidate for the PPC profile to the user (no default change\nin this round). Otherwise NO_GO. No retuning after the replay.\n",
